  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Monique. You're verified. I checked the delivery records for each of your recent orders, and here's what I found:\n\n**Saffron Lane (K-6501, today):** Credited $25.00\n- It was promised for 6:00 PM and handed to you at 6:52 PM, so it was 52 minutes late.\n- For deliveries 45 or more minutes late, you get 20% of the subtotal as credit. That would be $25.60, but the maximum for Plus members is $25.00, so you got $25.00.\n\n**Pho Real (K-6502, Oct 22):** Credited $5.00\n- It was promised for 7:15 PM and handed to you at 7:45 PM, so it was 30 minutes late.\n- For 16\u201344 minutes late, Plus members get $5.00 in credit.\n\n**Taqueria Luz (K-6503, Oct 20):** Not eligible\n- At 5:50 PM, 40 minutes before the original 6:30 PM delivery time, we sent you a push notification moving the delivery time to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage.\n- Since we told you that far in advance, 7:00 PM counts as the promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, which is within our 15-minute grace period, so it doesn't count as late.\n\n**Burger Barn (K-6504, Oct 16):** Not eligible\n- This one was 60 minutes late. But you can only request compensation for a late delivery within 7 days of when it arrived, and it arrived on Oct 16 at 8:00 PM, more than 7 days ago. Unfortunately I can't credit it.\n\n**Total: $30.00 in credit**, now in your account balance. You can use it on future orders. Late deliveries are compensated with credit only, not refunds to your card.\n\nI'm sorry this week's deliveries weren't up to standard. Is there anything else I can help you with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for checking. I'm not happy that Taqueria Luz and Burger Barn don't count, though. For Taqueria Luz, I never saw a notification like that. I only got the change when the app showed the new time, so I don't think it was sent to me at 5:50. Can you tell me why it doesn't count, and whether you can look at that again?\n\nFor Burger Barn, that order was an hour late. I was waiting on a delivery I'd paid for, so I'm not sure why the 7-day window matters if it's the company that was late. I'd like you to look at that one again too.\n\nI'm also still missing the summer rolls from Pho Real, #6502. Those were in the order and never arrived. I'd like them credited to my account."
  },
